  "title": "Change font size and contrast – Knowledge Base",
  "text": "Knowledge Base\nDaylio FAQ\nTutorials\nCreate and manage moods\nAdd note to entry\nAdd and manage photos\nSet up and track goals in Daylio\nChange font size and contrast\nChange language, the start of the week, or time format\nClear all data\nDelete account\nMove Daylio to new phone\nExport PDF\nWriting entries on computer\nUse multiple devices\nBackup and restore\nPurchases\nIssues\nAbout\nAll Docs\nAll Docs\nDaylio FAQ\nPopular Searches\nWordPress\nFooter\nLorem\nHome\nDaylio FAQ\nTutorials\nChange font size and contrast\n Updated on December 20, 2024\nDaylio FAQ\nTutorials\nCreate and manage moods\nAdd note to entry\nAdd and manage photos\nSet up and track goals in Daylio\nChange font size and contrast\nChange language, the start of the week, or time format\nClear all data\nDelete account\nMove Daylio to new phone\nExport PDF\nWriting entries on computer\nUse multiple devices\nBackup and restore\nPurchases\nIssues\nAbout\nChange font size and contrast\nEstimated reading: 2 minutes\n 5377 views\n\nAndroid and iOS have both built-in native tools for making your installed apps more usable. You can set the size and weight of fonts, use high contrast colors or color corrections, and many other tools.\n\nAndroid\nYou can change your font and display size to make your screen easier to see\nNote: Daylio does not have universal support for font size at this point. You can also use the settings to improve readability.\nSamsung has a Screen zoom setting that can be used. You can find it in phone settings under the Display menu.\nHigh contrast makes text easier to read on your device. This feature fixes the text color as either black or white, depending on the original text color.\nColor correction setting helps your device compensate for color blindness.\nDo you need to enlarge the screen only sometimes? You can use magnification to see your Android device’s screen better.\niOS\n\niOS has a nice presentation on accessibility features at https://www.apple.com/accessibility/. Apple offers a wide range of tools that can make your experience better. We encourage you to take control of your device and set it up how you prefer.\n\nIf you find your current UI small and would prefer bigger buttons, pictures, and text, you can switch your screen to a zoomed view.\n\nGo to iPhone Settings > Display & Brightness.\nTap View (below Display Zoom).\nChoose Zoomed, then tap Set.\n\n Still stuck? How can we help?\n\nWas this page helpful? Yes 2 No 2\n\nShare this Doc\nA-\nA\nA+\n CONTENTS\nAndroid\niOS\n\nPowered By EazyDocs\n\n© 2025 All Rights Reserved by Daylio",
